[? if social_liberal_coalition_heartland >= 45: We have enough votes to continue the "<span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span>-[? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Liberal</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">Liberal</span>?] Coalition" government between the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> and [? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #C0A054;">**Golds**</span>?][? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?]. ?][? if social_liberal_coalition_heartland < 45: We are able to stay in control of Heartland maintaining the "<span style="color: #c00000;">Social</span>-[? if not lvp_formed: <span style="color: #D3C24D;">Liberal</span>?][? if lvp_formed: <span style="color: #FFCC00;">Liberal</span>?] Coalition" government for the time being despite the lack of a majority. The recently instituted constructive vote of no confidence will allow our government to stay in power until another majority coalition agrees on a unified candidate for Minister-President, which is unlikely. ?][? if liberal_parliament == 1: The liberal parliamentary group has come under strain to the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span> acting on its own accord. ?] 

