[? if grand_coalition_heartland >= 45: Although we lack a simple majority in the state Assembly, we remain in power thanks to the toleration of the various regionalist parties. ?][? if grand_coalition_heartland < 45: We remain in power for now, albeit unpopular. However, there is a risk that the conservative establishment may call for a <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> against our government. The Unity Coalition parties have amended state Assembly rules to require an absolute majority to elect a new Minister-President, enabling [+ heartland_leader +] to continue ruling as a caretaker government indefinitely. An attempt to repeal the change is unexpectedly blocked by the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, effectively making them a de facto tolerator of [+ heartland_leader +]. [? if far_right_coalition_heartland + unionist_r_heartland >= 50: Furthermore, the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span> has engaged in delicate negotiations with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> over their potential entry into state government. However, despite being an enticing offer, it remains unlikely they would enter without also securing federal participation, as well as control over the Minister-President’s office and the Heartland police—demands the <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span> will never accept. ?]?] [? if heartland_leader != "Bristol": [+ heartland_leader +] is selected to be the Minister-President of Heartland. ?]

@far_right_coalition_prussia
title: <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Far</span>-[? if not dnf_formed:<span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span>?][? if dnf_formed:<span style="color: #003755;">right</span>?] Coalition
subtitle: <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span> + [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> ?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span> ?] ([+ far_right_coalition_heartland +]%)
view-if: far_right_coalition_heartland >= 50
on-arrival: in_far_right_coalition_heartland = 1; coup_progress += 5; landed_royalist += 10; commons_royalist += 10; burgher_royalist += 10; guild_royalist += 10; disfavored_royalist += 10; commons_marcher -= 5; commons_collectivist -= 5; heartland_leader = "Gorrick"; warden_strength += 100; warden_militancy += 0.1; loyalist_strength += 200; loyalist_militancy += 0.1; vanguard_banned = 1; vanguard_strength -= 50; banner_strength -= 200; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.5

There are enough votes for the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> and the [? if traditionalist_ideology == "Radical": <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Traditionalists**</span> ?][? if traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate": <span style="color: #003755;">**CNF**</span> ?] to form a coalition. Ulric Gorrick is elevated to the position of Minister-President and immediately starts dismantling its democratic institutions.

A wave of terror and repression unfolds, targeting the <span style="color: #c00000;">Reformists</span> and <span style="color: #700000;">collectivists</span>. Violence erupts in the streets, with bullets flying and leftists being killed or imprisoned.

@left_coalition_prussia
title: Is a United Left coalition possible?
subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> + <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> [? if sapd_formed: + <span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span> ?] ([+ left_coalition_heartland +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">Marchers</span> + <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span> [? if sapd_formed: + <span style="color: #9B0000;">Laborists</span> ?] ([+ left_coalition_heartland +]%). [? if collectivist_relation < 50 : We do not have adequate relations with the <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span>. ?][? if communist_coalition < 3 : The <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span> are too committed to their radical ways to partake in government. ?] [? if (president_ideology == "Right" or president == "DuFour") and not presidential_powers: [+ president +] will perform a <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> upon our government. ?] [? if reformist_strength >= left_strength: Our own Heartland party has ruled out this possibility. ?]
view-if: left_coalition_heartland >= 50
choose-if: (collectivist_relation >= 50 or (collectivist_leader == "Conciliators" and collectivist_relation >= 40)) and communist_coalition >= 3 and ((president_ideology != "Right" and president != "DuFour") or presidential_powers) and left_strength >= reformist_strength
on-arrival: in_left_front_heartland = 1; heartland_leader = "Pendrigon"; army_loyalty -= 0.05; gold_right += 5; ddp_right += 3; ddp_cohesion -= 2; lvp_right += 3; liberal_cooperation += 5; bourgeois_cooperation += 10; collectivist_relation += 10; unionist_relation -= 4; ddp_relation -= 4; lvp_relation -= 8; gold_relation -= 8; coup_progress += 2; coup_progress += 1 if in_left_front; capital_strike_progress += 2; capital_strike_progress += 1 if in_left_front; reformist_dissent += 25; reformist_strength -= 15; left_dissent -= 15; left_strength += 15; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.1; vanguard_strength += 50; vanguard_militancy += 0.05; marcher_heartland = 1
go-to: kpd_goals_prussia

Somehow, surprisingly, the left coalition is successfully formed, without appointing a <span style="color: #700000;">collectivist</span> as Minister-President. The consensus choice for Minister-President, accepted by the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>, is[? if left_split == 1:&nbsp;<span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span> member?] Cael Pendrigon, who [? if left_split == 0: belongs?][? if left_split == 1: belonged?] to the left faction of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, and had a history of defending <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> members through his work.

In response to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>'s entrance into the government, the right-wing takes a "wait-and-see" approach for now. They expect that our government will be unstable and incompetent, and will collapse of its own accord, eventually enabling the destruction of the Unity Republic. [? if in_left_front: The right will be more active in resisting our rule considering we are also ruling with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> on the federal level too. ?]

@popular_front_coalition_prussia
title: A new "Popular Front" coalition?
subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> + <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> + <span style="color: #000000;">**[+ unionist_party_name +]**</span>[? if liberal_parliament = 0 and not lvp_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #D3C24D;">**[+ ddp_name +]**</span>?][? if sapd_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span>?] ([+ popular_front_coalition_heartland +]%)
unavailable-subtitle: <span style="color: #c00000;">Marchers</span> + <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span> + <span style="color: #000000;">[+ unionist_party_name +]</span>[? if liberal_parliament = 0 and not lvp_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span>?][? if sapd_formed:&nbsp;+ <span style="color: #9B0000;">Laborists</span>?] ([+ popular_front_coalition_heartland +]%) - [? if ((collectivist_relation < 65 and collectivist_leader == "Halsmark") or (collectivist_relation < 45 and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators")) or ((unionist_leader == "Hawkins" and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators" and collectivist_relation < 35) or (unionist_leader == "Stilling" and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators" and collectivist_relation < 30)): We do not have good enough relations with the <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span>. ?][? if (unionist_relation < 45 and unionist_leader == "Hawkins") or (unionist_relation < 40 and unionist_leader == "Stilling") or (unionist_relation < 65 and unionist_ideology == "Right" and collectivist_leader != "Conciliators") or (unionist_relation < 55 and unionist_ideology == "Right" and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators") or ((unionist_leader == "Hawkins" and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators" and unionist_relation < 35) or (unionist_leader == "Stilling" and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators" and unionist_relation < 30)): We do not have good enough relations with the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?]. ?][? if (ddp_relation < 50 and ddp_ideology != "Left") or (ddp_relation < 40 and ddp_ideology == "Left") and liberal_parliament == 0 and not lvp_formed: We do not have good enough relations with the <span style="color: #D3C24D;">[+ ddp_name +]</span>. ?][? if communist_coalition < 3 : The <span style="color: #700000;">Collectivists</span> are unwilling to compromise at all. ?]
view-if: popular_front_coalition_heartland >= 50 and not concord_formed
choose-if: (((collectivist_relation >= 65 and collectivist_leader == "Halsmark") or (collectivist_relation >= 45 and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators")) and ((unionist_relation >= 45 and unionist_leader == "Hawkins") or (unionist_relation >= 40 and unionist_leader == "Stilling") or (unionist_relation >= 65 and unionist_ideology == "Right" and collectivist_leader != "Conciliators") or (unionist_relation >= 55 and unionist_ideology == "Right" and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators")) and ((liberal_parliament = 1 or lvp_formed) or ((ddp_relation >= 50 and ddp_ideology != "Left") or (ddp_relation >= 40 and ddp_ideology == "Left"))) and communist_coalition >= 3) or (unionist_leader == "Hawkins" and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators" and unionist_relation >= 35 and collectivist_relation >= 35) or (unionist_leader == "Stilling" and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators" and unionist_relation >= 30 and collectivist_relation >= 30)

Could we really form a coalition that included both the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>? It seems like an absurd concept, but given our good relationships with both sides, it is not an impossibility.

[? if president == "DuFour": DuFour might object to this, and may perform a <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> on our government, if such a coalition is formed.?]

- @popular_front_2: Form the Popular Front!
- @great_popular_front: Form the Popular Front!

@popular_front_2
view-if: unionist_ideology != "Left" or collectivist_leader != "Conciliators"

Somehow, both the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> and [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] are at the very least willing to entertain negotiations. Of course, <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> radicals and [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] conservatives derail the negotiations almost immediately. The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> demands leadership of the coalition for themselves, [? if marcher_r_heartland > collectivist_r_heartland : despite our higher vote share, ?]while the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] is offended by the prospect of helping <span style="color: #700000;">**revolutionaries**</span> enter government. Memories of the <i>Commonwealth intervention</i> against similar governments in Stathmore and Dornwich remain vivid, standing as a cautionary tale.

*Something* must be done to restore balance.

- @popular_front_resources
- @popular_front_democracy
- @popular_front_braun
- @coalition_menu: This is impossible. Try another governing arrangement.

@popular_front_resources
title: Use our resources to smooth things over.
unavailable-subtitle: Required: 3 resources
subtitle: -3 resources
choose-if: resources >= 3
on-arrival: resources -= 3
go-to: popular_front_success

@popular_front_democracy
title: Convince the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> to accept democracy.
subtitle: [? if collectivist_leader == "Conciliators" : The Conciliator leadership of the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> at least claim to support the Popular Front. ?]
unavailable-subtitle: Our relationship with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> is not high enough.
choose-if: (collectivist_relation >= 60 and communist_coalition >= 3) or collectivist_leader == "Conciliators"
go-to: popular_front_success

@popular_front_braun
title: Use pressure from President [+ president +] to force the parties to cooperate.
view-if: president_ideology == "Left"
go-to: popular_front_success

@popular_front_success
on-arrival: in_popular_front_heartland = 1; heartland_leader = "Pendrigon"; gold_right += 3; ddp_right += 2; ddp_cohesion -= 1.5 if liberal_parliament = 0; lvp_right += 3; liberal_cooperation += 3 if liberal_parliament = 1; liberal_cooperation += 2 if (liberal_parliament = 1 and in_popular_front or in_left_front); bourgeois_cooperation += 3; bourgeois_cooperation += 2 if in_popular_front or in_left_front; gold_relation -= 5; lvp_relation -= 5; collectivist_relation += 8; ddp_relation -= 5 if liberal_parliament = 1; coup_progress += 1; coup_progress += 1 if in_popular_front; reformist_dissent += 20; reformist_strength -= 10; left_dissent -= 10; left_strength += 10; ddp_in_popular_front_heartland = 1 if liberal_parliament = 0; vanguard_strength += 50; vanguard_militancy += 0.05; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.1; marcher_heartland = 1
go-to: kpd_goals_prussia

Somehow, surprisingly, the coalition is successfully formed! We still need a Minister-President; the only acceptable choice among the parties was [? if left_split == 1:&nbsp;<span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span> member?] Cael Pendrigon, who [? if left_split == 0: belongs?][? if left_split == 1: belonged?] to the left faction of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, and had a history of defending <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> members through his work. He is accepted with great reluctance to the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and welcomed by the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

In response to the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>'s entrance into the government, the right-wing takes a "wait-and-see" approach for now. They expect that the Popular Front government will be unstable and incompetent, and will collapse of its own accord, discrediting the left and center and eventually enabling the destruction of the Unity Republic. Our task is to prove them wrong. [? if in_left_front: The right will be more active in resisting our rule considering we are also ruling with the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> on the federal level too. ?]

@great_popular_front
view-if: unionist_ideology == "Left" and collectivist_leader == "Conciliators"
on-arrival: collectivist_relation += 5; unionist_relation += 5; ddp_relation += 5 if (liberal_parliament == 0 and not lvp_formed)
go-to: popular_front_success

Somehow, the coalition is successfully formed! The conciliatory leadership of the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> helped make the negotiations possible. We still need a Minister-President; the only acceptable choice among the parties was[? if left_split == 1:&nbsp;<span style="color: #9B0000;">**Laborists**</span> member?] Cael Pendrigon, who [? if left_split == 0: belongs?][? if left_split == 1: belonged?] to the left faction of the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span>, and had a history of defending <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> members through his work. He is accepted with great reluctance to the [? if unionist_party_name != "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">Unionists</span>?][? if unionist_party_name == "Concord": <span style="color: #000000;">**Concord**</span>?] and welcomed by the <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span>.

@kpd_goals_prussia
on-arrival: collectivist_goals_seen_heartland = 1; interior_goal_heartland = 0; bureaucracy_goal_heartland = 1; bureaucracy_goal_seen_heartland = 1; free_collectivist_goal_heartland = 1; free_collectivist_goal_seen_heartland = 1; vanguard_goal_heartland = 0; interior_goal_heartland = 1 if (loyalist_banned == 0 or warden_banned == 0); interior_goal_heartland = 2 if (loyalist_banned == 0 and warden_banned == 0); interior_goal_seen_heartland = 1 if (loyalist_banned == 0 or warden_banned == 0); vanguard_goal_heartland = 1 if vanguard_banned == 1; vanguard_goal_seen_heartland = 1 if vanguard_banned == 1; collectivist_ultimatum_heartland_timer = 24
go-to: popular_front_success_federal if heartland_negotiations_collectivist_trigger == 1; left_front_success_federal if heartland_negotiations_collectivist_left_trigger == 1

The <span style="color: #700000;">**Collectivists**</span> presents us with a list of demands for the Heartland coalition:

[? if interior_goal_heartland >= 1 : - Ban the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Loyalists**</span> and <span style="color: #3E88B3;">**Wardens**</span>. ?]

[? if vanguard_goal_heartland = 1 : - Unban the <span style="color: #700000;">**Vanguard**</span>. ?]

[? if bureaucracy_goal_heartland = 1 : - Purge the bureaucracy. ?]

[? if free_collectivist_goal_heartland = 1 : - Protect <span style="color: #700000;">collectivist</span> demonstrations. ?]

They say that they expect to see these goals fulfilled in [+ collectivist_ultimatum_heartland_timer +] months. Otherwise, they will vote to dissolve the coalition.

