@call_new_elections
subtitle: New elections will be called.
view-if: (((grand_coalition_heartland < 50) or ((grand_coalition_heartland >= 50 and (((gold_relation < 40 or gold_ideology == "Right") and not lvp_formed) or ((lvp_relation < 40 or lvp_ideology == "Right") and lvp_formed) or unionist_relation < 35)))) and far_right_coalition_heartland < 50 and (center_right_coalition_heartland < 50 or ((center_right_coalition_heartland >= 50 and ((traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" and not traditionalist_westarp) or (year = 1929 and month >= 7)))) and (right_coalition_heartland < 50 or (right_coalition_heartland >= 50 and ((traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" and not traditionalist_westarp) or (year = 1929 and month >= 7)))))) and not rubicon
go-to: call_new_elections_2 if no_majority_elections_heartland < 1 or (neo_weimar_coalition_heartland + kvp_r_heartland < 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Radical") or (neo_weimar_coalition_heartland + traditionalist_r_heartland < 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"); toleration_dilemma if no_majority_elections_heartland >= 1 and ((neo_weimar_coalition_heartland + kvp_r_heartland >= 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Radical") or (neo_weimar_coalition_heartland + traditionalist_r_heartland >= 50 and traditionalist_ideology == "Moderate"))

@toleration_dilemma

There is no path to a majority government. One option would be to tolerate a broad propertied government, without cabinet participation from the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Marchers**</span> at all. This is the only viable option for a government, as the propertied parties refuse to cooperate with us in any other capacity.

Otherwise, new elections have to be called, where the extremist parties stand to gain.

- @call_new_elections_2: We will have new elections.
- @tolerate_bourgeois_coalition: Tolerate the propertied parties to prevent new elections.

@call_new_elections_2
on-arrival: pro_republic -= 5 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; commons_royalist += 3 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; commons_collectivist += 3 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; commons_marcher -= 3 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; burgher_royalist += 2 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; guild_royalist += 2 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; landed_royalist += 2 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; burgher_ddp -= 2 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; guild_ddp -= 2 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; landed_ddp -= 2 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; burgher_gold -= 2 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; guild_gold -= 2 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; landed_gold -= 2 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; burgher_lvp -= 2 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; guild_lvp -= 2 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; landed_lvp -= 2 if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30; no_majority_elections_heartland += 1; next_election_week_heartland = next_election_week if rubicon and next_election_time - time < 3; next_election_week_heartland = week + 6 if rubicon and next_election_time - time >= 3; next_election_week_heartland -= 4 if rubicon and next_election_week_heartland > 4; next_election_week_heartland -= 4 if rubicon and next_election_week_heartland > 4
call: set_next_election_time_prussia

[? if far_right_coalition_heartland + unionist_r_heartland >= 50: The <span style="color: #000000;">Unionist Party</span>'s failure to form a coalition with the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">**Royalists**</span>, due to the latter's insistence on securing both the Minister-President's office and control of the Heartland police, has left no alternative but to call new elections. ?]

New Heartland elections have been set for [+ next_election_month_heartland : month +] [+ next_election_year_heartland + 2365 +][? if rubicon:, Week [+ next_election_week +] ?].

[? if anti_democratic_coalition_heartland >= 30: The people's faith in democracy is shaken by this ordeal. Of course, the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">Royalists</span> are exploiting the instability to claim that democracy is unworkable, and that the Commonwealth needs a strong leader. ?]

@tolerate_bourgeois_coalition
title: We must tolerate a propertied coalition.
on-arrival: heartland_leader = "Sedgewick" if unionist_leader != "Sedgewick"; heartland_leader = "Askew" if unionist_leader == "Sedgewick"; heartland_leader = "Lytton" if (gold_leader == "Lytton" or lvp_leader == "Lytton" and lvp_formed); marcher_toleration_heartland = 1; burgher_marcher -= 4; ddp_right += 1; ddp_cohesion -= 1; gold_right += 1; lvp_right += 1; center_dissent += 5; left_dissent += 10; heartland_police_loyalty -= 0.05; heartland_police_strength -= 10; pro_republic -= 3; right_heartland = 1

We have decided to tolerate a broad propertied government. This means that we will vote against no-confidence votes to make sure they fail, but also that we will not be directly participating as ministers in the government. Thus, we can prevent a new election and stop the <span style="color: #7A3C00;">far</span> <span style="color: #3E88B3;">right</span> from entering government.

[? if heartland_leader != "Bristol": [+ heartland_leader +] is selected to be the Minister-President of Heartland. ?]

@call_new_elections_rubicon
subtitle: New elections will be called.
view-if: (((grand_coalition_heartland < 50) or ((grand_coalition_heartland >= 50 and (gold_relation < 40 or (lvp_relation < 40 and lvp_formed) or unionist_relation < 35)))) and far_right_coalition_heartland < 50 and (center_right_coalition_heartland < 50 or ((center_right_coalition_heartland >= 50 and ((traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" and not traditionalist_westarp) or (year = 1929 and month >= 7)))) and (right_coalition_heartland < 50 or (right_coalition_heartland >= 50 and ((traditionalist_ideology == "Radical" and not traditionalist_westarp) or (year = 1929 and month >= 7)))))) and rubicon
on-arrival: no_majority_elections_heartland_staal = 1
go-to: call_new_elections_2_rubicon if heartland_leader != "Bristol" and heartland_leader != "Sedgewick" and heartland_leader != "Lytton" and heartland_leader != "Askew"; prussia_explode if heartland_leader == "Bristol" or heartland_leader == "Sedgewick" or heartland_leader == "Lytton" or heartland_leader == "Askew"

@call_new_elections_2_rubicon
view-if: gnu_r_heartland < 50 and (staal_right_coalition_heartland < 50 or dsu_leader == "Corin Crowde")
on-arrival: next_election_week_heartland = next_election_week if rubicon and next_election_time - time < 3; next_election_week_heartland = week + 6 if rubicon and next_election_time - time >= 3; next_election_week_heartland -= 4 if rubicon and next_election_week_heartland > 4; next_election_week_heartland -= 4 if rubicon and next_election_week_heartland > 4
call: set_next_election_time_prussia

Perhaps a more stable majority can be found in more elections.

New Heartland elections have been set for [+ next_election_month_heartland : month +] [+ next_election_year_heartland + 2365 +], Week [+ next_election_week +].

@prussia_explode
go-to: prussian_coup_schleicher